  "Mojo-E died on dungeon level 33 [max 50] (with the Amulet)"

 That's bad enough on its own, but what really pisses me off is that I
shouldn't have died.  The story: I was on my way up, making pretty good
time, killing everything in sight with few problems (-28AC, or -23 if I was
wearing my levitation boots, which was most of the time, +6 Mjollnir).  
So I get to level 33, I'm looking for a staircase up, and I find a magic
trap (My luck is maxed out and I have a blessed luckstone, so I find most
traps before I hit them).  I figure, no problem, I'm levitating so I won't
trip it.  BZZZT, wrong answer, but I suppose that makes sense; a magic
field could affect anybody who wandered into the square.  I'd lost my 
telepathy a long time ago, so I didn't know what I was fighting, I just
killed it and kept walking along the corridor.  Bad mistake.  I get my
sight back a few moves later, and things look quiet, so I keep looking
for the stairs.  Suddenly, a pit fiend comes up behind me and grabs me.  
I wield Demonbane and start to hack at him, but before I kill him, he
summons another one, on the other side of me in the corridor.  I kill
the first one, and another takes his place, and _he_ summons another one
(this is at a T intersection, like this).

    ---
     &&
    |@|
    |&|

  Now, one of them grabs me.  I have no way of knowing which one, so I take
a guess.  "You cannot escape from the pit fiend!  The pit fiend hits! The 
pit fiend hits!" etc.  
  This is stupid.  I can sorta see an argument for making an attempt to
get away from something that's holding you take a turn (while you're
struggling, it gets a chance to hit you), but it's ridiculous to *not know
which one is holding you*.  Either trying to move away from something that's
holding you shouldn't take a turn, or there should be an easy way to know
which one is holding you.  

  Qualm #2.  Identify should work a lot better.  Let's say I have three
things in my inventory I'm interested in.  
Z-a pine amulet   (REALLY want to know if it's strangulation or life saving)
Y-a diamond ring  (would like to know if it's something interesting)
X-a blessed warhammer named Mjollnir  (would be nice to know what the
				       enchantment is). 

Now, clearly, I want to identify these things in reverse order, and there's
no logical reason that I shouldn't be able to based on what pack slots I
had open when I picked them up.  Identify should work more like 'I'--it
asks you what kind of thing you want to identify (I press "), then 
give you a listing (Identify which [adZ]?).  If I can still identify more
items, it goes back to the same prompt (Identify which [adZ]?).  If I
don't enter one, it goes back to (Identify which kind of item ")[!=?().  
I think putting things into bags should also work this way, although
that doesn't affect game play.  But it's annoying to have to scroll
through your entire inventory list when you only want to put one item
in a bag.
 -Tom


